  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fostering digital democracy in Indonesia to ensure sustainable civil freedom protection through inclusive digital governance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Massive and systemic spread and impact of disinformation especially in political context needs to be responded by a comprehensive approach to ensure democratic governance exists in the digital space. This requires regulatory approach as well as building digitally informed masses to counter the trend. The purpose of this project is to strengthen public participation, particularly civil society groups, and youth to foster digital democracy in Indonesia that sustains civil freedom protection, through the development of inclusive digital governance. Increased public participation by the two target groups in this project can be measured from several aspects, such as: the quantity of their public participation in various digital citizenship capacity building activities to be organised under the project ; increased intensity of conversations and public involvement in various public issues, including in the social media space; publicly available relevant campaign materials and tools related to digital citizenship; and the accommodation of The purpose of this project is to strengthen public participation, particularly civil society groups, and youth to foster digital democracy in Indonesia that sustains civil freedom protection, through the development of inclusive digital governance. Increased public participation by the two target groups in this project can be measured from several aspects, such as: the quantity of their public participation in various digital citizenship capacity building activities to be organised under the project ; increased intensity of conversations and public involvement in various public issues, including in the social media space; publicly available relevant campaign materials and tools related to digital citizenship; and the accommodation of public interests and aspirations in various policy processes and substances related to digital governance.</narrative>
  </description>
